  "seminaryName": "St. Patrick's Seminary and University",
  "voice": {
    "weather": [
      "Summer is fog until noon in the Sunset and sun all day in Marin, and the pastor learns to bring a coat to every wedding.",
      "The one warm week comes in October, and the whole city acts as if it were a miracle, which in the Richmond it is.",
      "Winter is rain in long grey sheets from Advent to Lent, and the leak in the sacristy is a member of the parish council.",
      "Earthquake weather is not a thing, the seismologists say, and every pastor over sixty knows better."
    ],
    "sunday": [
      "The Filipino Mass in Daly City fills the church and the lot and a second building, and the collection is counted by a committee of aunties.",
      "In Marin the ushers are retired executives and the collection is by app; in the Mission it is cash and a raffle for someone's surgery.",
      "The nine-thirty in the Sunset is Irish widows and Chinese grandmothers who do not share a language and share a pew."
    ],
    "presbyterate": [
      "The priests of San Francisco are few enough to know each other's opinions and old enough to keep them to dinner.",
      "Half of them went to Menlo Park and the other half came from somewhere warmer, and the difference shows in the vestments.",
      "They know the real estate value of every church in the city and speak of it the way farmers speak of rain."
    ]
  },
